<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">16 May in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">5 events that happened on 16 May, from 1532 to 1960.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1532 CE <span class="tih-ago">494 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Thomas More resigns as Lord Chancellor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A day after the clergy submitted to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-viii-of-england">Henry VIII</a>'s authority, Sir Thomas More gave up the Great Seal. His refusal to accept the king's supremacy over the Church led to his execution in 1535.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/marie-antoinette" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marie-antoinette.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1770 CE <span class="tih-ago">256 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marie Antoinette marries the future Louis XVI</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The fourteen-year-old Austrian archduchess married the French dauphin at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a>, sealing an alliance between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbons</a>. Both were guillotined during the Revolution.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1868 CE <span class="tih-ago">158 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Andrew Johnson escapes conviction by one vote</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Senate voted 35 to 19 to convict President Johnson on the first article tried, one vote short of the two-thirds needed. Johnson was the first US president to be impeached.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1929 CE <span class="tih-ago">97 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Academy Awards are presented in Hollywood</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">About 270 guests attended a dinner at the Hollywood Roosevelt Hotel where the first Oscars were handed out in around fifteen minutes. Wings won the top prize.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1960 CE <span class="tih-ago">66 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Theodore Maiman operates the first laser</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Hughes Research Laboratories in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a>, Maiman produced a pulse of red laser light from a ruby crystal. Lasers went on to transform medicine, communications and industry.</p></div></li></ol>
